        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "You\u2019re already on a great track \ud83d\udd25 asparagus + butter + Cajun + garlic = solid base. Now let\u2019s elevate it into *restaurant-level*:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd25 Flavor Boosters (pick 2\u20134 of these)\n\n### \ud83e\uddc2 Acid (THIS is what most people miss)\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"lemon wedge squeezing over asparagus\",\"balsamic glaze drizzle asparagus\",\"red wine vinegar cooking\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n- Fresh **lemon juice** at the end (game changer)\n- Splash of **balsamic glaze**\n- Tiny dash of **red wine vinegar**\n\n\ud83d\udc49 This cuts the butter and makes everything pop\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddc0 Rich + Savory\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"parmesan cheese grated over asparagus\",\"pecorino romano cheese close up\",\"butter garlic asparagus skillet\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n- **Fresh grated parmesan** (don\u2019t skip this)\n- Or **pecorino romano** for stronger flavor\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf36\ufe0f Heat + Depth\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"red pepper flakes close up\",\"smoked paprika spice\",\"cajun sausage sliced skillet\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n- Pinch of **red pepper flakes**\n- Little **smoked paprika**\n- Or throw in sliced **andouille sausage** if you want it hearty\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf3f Fresh Finish (makes it taste \u201cchef-level\u201d)\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"fresh parsley chopped garnish asparagus\",\"thyme leaves close up\",\"green onions chopped garnish\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n- **Fresh parsley**\n- **Thyme**\n- Or **green onions**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddc4 Bonus Upgrades\n- Add **minced shallots or onions** at the start\n- Toss in **cherry tomatoes** for sweetness\n- Finish with a drizzle of **olive oil** for shine\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd11 Pro Move (this is what makes it AMAZING)\nCook asparagus until slightly crispy \u2192 turn off heat \u2192 add:\n- squeeze of lemon  \n- parmesan  \n- tiny bit more butter  \n\nLet it melt together for 30 seconds\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a *full 10-minute chef-style recipe* with exact measurements so it hits every time."
          ]
